SignetMail Licence Agreement (EULA)

Copyright (c) 2026 Aljaž Eferl. All rights reserved.

SignetMail (the "Software") is proprietary software. It is provided in binary form
(container image, installer) and is NOT open source. Source code is not published.

1. Free use. You may install and use the Software free of charge, with all features
   and without time limit, if your organization (together with its affiliates) has no
   more than 50 active users. An active user is a person who received an e-mail
   signature generated by the Software within the previous 30 days.

2. Larger organizations. If your organization has more than 50 active users you need
   a commercial licence (info@signetmail.si). Above the free limit without a licence the
   Software keeps delivering signatures, but shows a reminder and disables the Pro
   features (campaigns, AI connections, rollout overview and user list). A commercial
   licence includes, for its term, updates and e-mail support on working days from
   8:00 to 16:00 (Central European Time).

3. Not allowed without written permission: (a) offering the Software, or functionality
   substantially similar to it, to third parties as a hosted or managed service,
   (b) selling, renting, sublicensing or redistributing the Software, (c) reverse
   engineering, decompiling or disassembling it except where the law does not allow
   this restriction, (d) removing licence notices, or the licence check and reminder.
   IT partners who install the Software for their customers need a partner licence.

4. Licence check. By accepting this agreement (installer, or first sign-in of the owner
   in the portal) you agree that the installation sends a licence check once a day to
   the author: a random installation ID, the version and a range for the number of active
   users. No names, e-mail addresses, domains or directory data are sent. The Software
   keeps working if the check cannot be sent (no lock, no internet requirement).

5. Ownership. The Software and the name SignetMail remain the property of the author.
   No trademark rights are granted.

6. No warranty. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the
   extent permitted by law the author is not liable for any damage arising from its use.

7. Termination. The licence ends automatically if you break these terms. Then you must
   stop using the Software and delete all copies.

8. Governing law: Republic of Slovenia. Courts in Maribor have jurisdiction, unless
   mandatory law provides otherwise.
